[Black "X-Ray Attacks"]
[Result "*"]
[FEN "kn6/pp6/3b4/4q3/8/6Q1/PP3P2/KN1R4 w - - 0 1"]
[SetUp "1"]

{ I will now present another motif to look out for. An X-ray attack refers to a situation where a long-range piece indirectly attacks an enemy piece through another piece or pieces. For example, in this position, the g3 Queen indirectly attacks the d6 Bishop through the e5 Queen. This brings the Bishop to a total of 2 attackers  (The d1 Rook and g3 Queen)  and only 1 defender  (The e5 Queen)  . Sure enough, a simple calculation shows that the Bishop is indeed hanging. }
1. Rxd6
{ By the same token, when one of your pieces seems unsalvageable, you can use X-ray defence to protect a friendly piece through an enemy piece. In this position, the g3 Queen is protecting the d6 Rook through the e5 Queen. }
1... Qxd6 2. Qxd6
{ Hence, when considering whether a piece is unprotected/hanging, aside from counting its direct attackers and defenders, be sure to include the indirect X-ray attacks and defences as well.  The subsequent puzzles will require you to identify targets using this motif. If you are still confused, don’t worry. We will start with two simple puzzles to further illustrate X-ray attacks and defences. }
*

