{ 1. Count the material and identify any material imbalance  2. Identify tactical motifs    a. Unprotected/hanging pieces    b. Existing/potential threats    c. X-Ray attacks   3. Calculate candidate moves.  Step 1: Black is up one pawn.   Step 2: The d4 Queen, c1 Rook, and e3 Knight are all unprotected. There is one more target on the board not listed above. Which one is it? It is the e4 Knight. The e4 Knight is unprotected, defended once by the d4 Queen and under an X-ray attack from White's b4 Queen.   Step 3: Keeping in mind that our two targets are the d4 Queen and the e4 Knight, what should we play here? }
1. Rc4
{ Skewering the two unprotected pieces. With two pieces @@StartBracket@@the b4 Queen and c4 Rook@@EndBracket@@ X-raying the e4 Knight, White will win the piece. }
