{ 1. Count the material and identify any material imbalance  2. Identify tactical motifs    a. Unprotected/hanging pieces    b. Existing/potential threats    c. X-Ray attacks   3. Calculate candidate moves.  Step 1: Black is up a pawn.   Step 2: The g8 Rook is hanging while all the other pieces are unprotected. White has a massive, immediate threat of Qxg8# while Black has a longer-term threat of queening the queenside pawns.   Step 3: Keeping in mind that we need to take care of our g8 Rook before we can promote our pawns, find a good defensive move }
1... Qc4
{ It may seem like the only way to save the g8 Rook is to take on e8, but that only gets us a draw. The text move, however, cleverly saves the day with an X-ray defence  If   1...Rxe8  White gets a draw  2.Qg6+  Kg8  3.Qxe8+  Kh7  4.Qg6+  Kg8  5.Qe8+ }
2. Qxg8+ { 2.Rxg8  Qxf7 } 2... Qxg8 3. Rxg8 Kxg8
{ Black will win thanks to his queenside pawns } *

