{ 1. Count the material and identify any material imbalance  2. Identify tactical motifs    a. Unprotected/hanging pieces    b. Existing/potential threats    c. X-Ray attacks   3. Calculate candidate moves.  Step 1: Material is equal.   Step 2: White threatens to take either Black's f6 Knight or d6 Bishop. These two  are the only hanging pieces on the board. The main unprotected spots are the g2 pawn and the b1 Knight.   Step 3: Find a few candidate moves that work with these targets. }
1... Nxd4
{ Although the b1 Knight is unprotected, there is no real way to add attackers or remove the defender. However, for g2, we do have our b7 Bishop giving an X-ray attack through the c6 Knight and the f3 Knight. By thinking of ways to get those two Knights out of the way, we find this powerful move. Black has far too many threats for White to handle such as Bxf3, Nxf3 and Nxe2. }
2. Nxd4 Qxg2# *

