{ Going beyond the earlier two basic motifs which are unprotected/hanging pieces and existing/potential threats, there is another one I’d like to introduce: Mating possibilities. Among its variations, the simplest pattern is a weak back rank. This refers to a situation where the defender has either one or no major piece guarding his back rank and has not moved any pawns in front of his King. Be sure to include this new motif in step 2 when solving the subsequent puzzles. }
