[Black "Critical Lines and Squares"]
[Result "*"]

{ In this final section of Chapter 1, we will look at critical lines and squares. Of all the concepts we have discussed, this one is the most complex and abstract. Critical lines and squares refer to files, ranks, diagonals, and squares that are extremely important in creating tactics. They encompass all the different tactical motifs we have gone through so far, from unprotected and forkable pieces to weak back ranks. Additionally, there are two new ones to be included. The first is squares on which your pieces can land to win material or deliver checkmate. The next is a weak file, rank, or diagonal towards a King.  After you have identified the critical lines and squares, you should mentally highlight them. The real difficulty is in deciding which are the most important lines and squares. As always, I will guide you closely at the start of the next few puzzles and draw your attention to these lines and squares. }
1. -- *

