Step 1: White has a Knight for Black's pawn.   Step 2: Only Black's g4 Rook is unprotected. This position does not seem to have any tactics. However, given that Black has doubled rooks on the file adjacent to the enemy monarch, the g-file is a critical line. Additionally, the g2 and g3 squares are critical because they are unprotected.   Step 3: Recognising this new type of tactical idea, find a few candidate moves and pick the best. }
