1. Re8+
{ Down a significant amount of material, the best plan to consider is a strong attack. }
1... Kd7 2. Qd8+ Kc6
{ I believe you would have reached this position in your calculation, where it is important to realise that Qd5 does not work }
3. Re6+
{ Black is forced to accept this sacrifice and commit to putting his Knight on e6, away from the defence of b5   3.Qd5+  Kb6  Qb5 is prevented, and after  4.Re6+  Black is not obliged to blunder by accepting your Rook here  4...c6   4...Nxe6  5.Qb5 }
3... Nxe6 { 3...Kc5  4.Qe7 } 4. Qd5+ Kb6
{ This is the same position from the line with 3. Qd5+and 4...Nxe6?? } 5. Qb5#
