[FEN "3r3k/pp5p/n1ppqp2/3b1N2/6PQ/2B5/P6P/6K1 w - - 1 1"]
[SetUp "1"]

1. Qh6
{ The idea is to threaten Qg7# first, then play Bxf6 with check.  My guess is that your first instinct is to play   1.Bxf6+  but after  1...Kg8  we discover that White does not truly have an attack  2.Ne7+   2.Qh6  We must leave at least one of the pieces @@StartBracket@@either our Qh4 or Bc3@@EndBracket@@ guarding e1  2...Qe1  Kf8  3.Qh6+  Ke8  And Black finds shelter on the Queenside }
1... Qf7 { Black must defend g7   1...Qd7  2.Qxf6+  Kg8  3.Nh6 } 2. Bxf6+ Kg8
3. Ne7+
{ 3.Ne7+  Qxe7  4.Qg5+  wins an extra Rook and is even more accurate than the immediate Bxe7  4...Kf8   4...Kf7  5.Qg7+  Qxe7# next  5.Bxe7+ }
