{ At the end of the combination, we will win his Queen back and this Rook is ours to keep. Meanwhile, Qd1+ is taken care of while Qg4+ can be met with Qg3.  At first glance, the only reasonable check here seems to be   1.Rc8+  Kf7  Forced. Again, we have no checks, so the natural continuation to consider is  2.Rf8+  Kg6  Here, our Rook has an X-ray attack on the f3 Queen. However, it is a pity we are unable to take advantage of that  3.Qxe5  Qd1+  Saving the Queen from Rxf3  4.Kg2  fxe5  Using reciprocal thinking, we discover that we simply need to switch the move order. }
