{ With an unstoppable threat of Rec7#  The motif is clearly some sort of King hunt. But with just about any first move other than Rb7, the Black King will escape to b8, then a8, where it will be very safe, since the a5 Rook defends a7.   1.Rc7+  Kb8  Arriving at the conclusion that b8 is the square to take away, Rb7 presents itself }
1... Rb5 2. Rec7#
