1. Bb2+ { 1.Nxf7  The Corner mate } 1... f6 2. Bxf6#
{ Morphy's mate   1. Piece interaction and responsibilities:   (i)  White Rook prevents the Black King from escaping to g7 or g8   (ii)  Black h7 pawn prevents the Black King from escaping to the last square, h7   (iii)  White Bishop/Knight delivers a check from a square that they cannot be blocked or captured, resulting in checkmate  2. Strategical weaknesses:   (i)  Black must have poor control over the g-file   (ii)  Black must have poor control over the b2-h8 diagonal  (For Morphy’s mate)    (iii)  f7 must not be defended at the starting position  (For Corner mate)   3a. Changes in the position that would make this particular combination fail:   (i)  Black has an additional Rook on f8    (ii)  Black h7 pawn is replaced by a Black Knight  (For Morphy’s mate)   3b. Changes in the position that would still allow the tactic to work:   (i)  Black h7 pawn is replaced by a Black Bishop }
