1. Rh8+ Kxh8 2. Qh1+ Kg8 3. Qh7#
{ 1. Piece interaction and responsibilities:   (i)  White g6 pawn covers f7 and h7   (ii)  White Queen delivers a checkmate by covering g8 and h8   (iii)  Black Rook prevents the Black King from escaping to f8  2. Strategical weaknesses:   (i)  Black must have weak light squares around the Black King   (ii)  h7 must not be defended at the starting position   (iii)  Black allowed the White pawn to reach g6, where it gives White strong attacking prospects  3a. Changes in the position that would make this particular combination fail:   (i)  Black Rook is replaced with a Knight   (ii)  Black Rook is not on its current square  3b. Changes in the position that would still allow the tactic to work:   (i)  Black g7 pawn is removed   (ii)  White g6 pawn is replaced with a White Bishop   (iii)  Black f8 Rook is replaced with any Black piece except a Knight }
