{ Now that you have applied PIE to the 10 mating patterns, you are armed with a new set of tactical motifs to work with. For example, when the Black King is castled Kingside and you have a White pawn on g6, you can consider ideas of the Damiano’s mate. Or if you have a fianchettoed White Bishop at b2 sniping at the Black King on g8, ideas of the Suffocation Mate or Lolli’s mate come to mind, among many others.   To put your newly acquired knowledge to the test, we will be attempting to solve some checkmating puzzles. Be sure to keep an eye for the new motifs we have covered from the previous patterns.   I will not be providing any hints. However, the explanations and ideal thought process to solve each puzzle will be revealed only after you have completed it. }
