[SetUp "1"]

exf3+ { This is an obvious candidate move to consider } 2. Kxf3 Qg4+
{ White's Kingside pawns all on dark squares and he has no light-squared Bishop. This makes his light squares are extremely weak. On top of that, with the Black pawn on h4, our newly heightened senses will tell us to look out for a Lolli's mate with the pawn potentially at h3 and the Queen at f3 }
3. Kg2 h3+ 4. Kg1 { 4.Kh1  Qf3+  5.Kg1  Qg2 } 4... Qf3
{ This simple puzzle illustrates how you can connect new patterns/motifs to solve positions. }
