1... Ra1+
{ With a Qg5+ looming and the f3 Knight controlling d2, this position resembles a smothered mate pattern but with all the pieces shifted one file towards the centre. Additionally, after   1...Qg5+  2.Kb1  Nd2+  3.Kxa2  this position resembles the Anastasia's mate pattern with Ra8, if not for the White Rook at a3.  Using reciprocal thinking, we realise that we should use our a2 Rook to divert the White a3 Rook from defending the King. }
2. Rxa1 Qg5+ 3. Kb1 Nd2+ 4. Kc1 Nb3+ 5. Kb1 Qc1+ 6. Rxc1 Nd2+
{ A pseudo-smothered mate that morphs into the Anastasia's mate } 7. Ka2 Ra8+
8. Qa6 Rxa6# *

