1. Qa3
{ Our Bishop on h6 strongly suggests that we have mating ideas on the dark squares. Looking at the position of the Black pieces, ideas of the Opera mate @@StartBracket@@with Qf8@@EndBracket@@ and Lolli's mate @@StartBracket@@Qf6 or Qg7#@@EndBracket@@ come to mind. Additionally, the critical square are f8, g7, and the critical diagonal is a1-g8. Hence, we arrive at the most efficient way to reroute our Queen to that critical diagonal. }
1... Qc5 { 1...Bd7  2.Qb2   2.Qe7  to play Qf6 next is also strong } 2. Qb2
{ Thanks to the e2 Knight which reinforces our control over the diagonal, 2. ...Qc3 is not possible defence by Black }
2... f6 3. Qxf6 Rd7
{ 3...Rd7  4.dxe6  Rdc7  5.Nf4  With Nd5, Rd1, and Qe5 looming, White's attack will be decisive }
