[FEN "r4rk1/1bp2pp1/p2bp2p/1p1n4/3P4/P1PQ2Pq/1PBBNP1P/R4RK1 b - - 0 1"]
[SetUp "1"]

1... Qg2+
{ This position is very sharp. White's light squares are very weak, especially with the Queen at h3 and the Bishop at b7. On the other hand, White is threatening an immediate Qh7#. This narrows our candidate moves to checks and defensive moves. Additionally, when looking out for familiar features in the position, we realise that we could have a Lolli's mate with a protected Queen at g2, or a Suffocation mate with the d5 Knight teleporting to h3. When considered together with the limit on our candidate moves, these two familiar patterns help uncover this beautiful combination. }
2. Kxg2 Nf4+
{ Double check! Stopping Kh3, while the Knight plans to go to h3 himself } 3.
Kg1 { Forced } 3... Nh3# *

