{ This is a blitz game played between Peter Svidler  (White)  and Magnus Carlsen  (Black)  . How did Svidler deal with the far-advanced passed c-pawn and the pesky Bishop pair? }
48. Rxh6+
{ An uncannily similar mating pattern to the one seen in the 2016 World Championships @@StartBracket@@Pattern #20@@EndBracket@@. Except for this time, Carlsen is the victim. The piece layout may not be obvious, so allow me to show how the two positions compare. The h5 pawn and b8 Rook serve the same purposes as they did in Carlsen - Karjakin. Svidler's g6 Rook taking on h6 is similar to Carlsen's Queen sacrificed on h6 in the game with Karjakin. }
48... Kxh6
{ 48...gxh6  49.Rh8  Here, Svidler does not have Rf7# as seen in Carlsen's game with Karjakin. Instead, Svidler's Bishop covers g7 takes care of the mate }
49. Rh8#
{ Here, instead of having an f5 Rook cover g5, the f4 pawn does the same job }
