{ It is very important to bear in mind that the pawn square technique CANNOT be applied if the pawn is on the second rank. This is because the pawn can still move two squares and will disrupt the elegant geometry and mathematics of the pawn square rule.   Instead, we need to calculate one move deeper, where the pawn would have left the second rank for the fourth rank and the King would have taken a step closer to the pawn.    Here, this scenario plays out. The Black King has just entered the pawn square. However, our pawn holds the trump card of the double move. }
1. h4 Kc5
{ Notice the King is now no longer in the box. This means that our pawn will score a touchdown. }
2. h5 Kd6 3. h6 Ke7 4. h7 Kf8 5. h8=Q+ *

