[FEN "8/8/1k6/8/P1P5/8/8/7K w - - 0 1"]
[SetUp "1"]

{ Even if the two passed pawns are separated by a file, they are still untouchable pawns. }
1. Kg2 Kc5 { Black is threatening to take on c4, how can we stop it? } 2. a5
{ The c4 pawn is now untouchable because when Black plays …Kxc4, we will push the a-pawn to victory. }
2... Kc6 { Let's see what happens if Black goes after the a-pawn instead. } 3.
Kf3 Kb7
{ Now ...Ka6 followed by ...Kxa5 is a strong threat. Since the idea is to meet ...Ka6 with c6, we should prepare that with c5 now }
4. c5
{ Yet again, the two pawns indirectly mutually defend each other. If the Black King attacks and captures one pawn, the other runs up the board. }
4... Ka6 5. c6
{ As the Black King approached the a-pawn, the c-pawn had made a run for it }
5... Kxa5 6. c7 *

