{ Strangely enough, passed pawns with exactly two files between them are NOT untouchable. This is because they are not quite far enough to keep the enemy King busy running from side to side  (Refer to Position 16)  . At the same time, they don't create a barrier to defend each other like the case of them separated by a single file  (Refer to Position 15)  . Hence, the defender can draw this. }
1. Kh5 e5 2. Kg4 Ka7 3. Kf5 h5 4. Kxe5 h4 5. Kf4 h3 6. Kg3 h2 7. Kxh2 *

