1. Qxf7+ Kxf7 2. h5
{ When pawns are untouchable, it merely means that they can hold off the enemy King. These pawns may need their King’s help to queen safely. However, they can sometimes queen on their own. Here is a rule to help you identify such cases: When two passed pawns are on the same rank, and they are at least as far from the promotion square as they are to each other, one of those pawns will queen.   Here, the pawn on e5 is just as far from its promotion square as it is from its compatriot on the h-file. This means at least one of those pawns will score a touchdown. }
2... Ke6 3. h6 Kxe5 { 3...Kf7  4.e6+  Kg6  5.e7  Kf7  6.h7 } 4. h7 Kf6 5. h8=Q+
*

