{ If the attacker has a bishop pawn or a central pawn, passive defence no longer works. Instead, we need to use the Philidor technique. The first step is to place our Rook on the third rank. This prevents the enemy King from advancing any further to threaten checkmate. }
1. Rh3
{ Passive defence does not work because Black can skewer our King and Rook from the other side.   1.Rh1  Ra1+ }
1... Ra1+ 2. Kd2 Ra2+ 3. Kd1 Kd5 4. Rg3 Kc4
{ 4...Ra7  5.Rh3  Rc7  6.Rg3  Ke4  7.Rh3  Rc3  8.Rxc3  dxc3  9.Kc2  Kd4  10.Kc1 }
5. Rh3 d3
{ Black may push his pawn to create a 3rd rank shield to threaten ...Kc3. When that happens, move the Rook to the last rank immediately and keeping checking your opponent from there. }
6. Rh8 Kc3 7. Rc8+ Kd4 8. Rd8+ Kc4 9. Rc8+ Kb5
{ If the Black King ever strays too far, go after the pawn. } 10. Rd8 Ra3 11.
Kd2 Kc4 12. Rc8+ Kd4 13. Rd8+ Ke4 14. Re8+ Kf5 15. Rd8 *

