{ Let's now take a look at a similar position where the defender's King is cut off by two files. This is a win. However, the White King and pawn alone still have no way of making progress by themselves. This is where the White Rook can help create a breakthrough. Unlike the previous position, the Black King requires too much time to get back into the scene. }
1. Kc4 Rc8+ 2. Kd5 Rd8+ 3. Kc5 Rc8+ 4. Kb6 Rd8 5. Rd1 Kf6
{ Had the White Rook only cut the Black King off by one file, the Black King would be at e6 by now and would easily draw the game. }
6. Kc7 Rd5 7. Kc6 Rd8 8. d5
{ White will soon convert this into a Lucena position @@StartBracket@@Position 20@@EndBracket@@. Any attempt by the Black King to get closer to his pawn now would be met with Re1+ }
8... Ke7 9. Re1+ Kf7 10. d6 Rc8+ 11. Kd7 Rc2 12. Kd8 Rc3 13. d7 *

