1. Rg2
{ This is a waiting move. Now Black's King must move to a worse square. } 1...
Kh4
{ Note that if at any time, Black plays   1...Kh6  the win is easy because mating ideas appear.  2.Kf4  Rf8+  3.Ke5  Re8+  4.Kf6  the e4 pawn is immune to capture because of Rh2+  4...Rf8+  5.Ke7  Ra8  6.e5  This is NOT the same as the short/long side defence @@StartBracket@@Position 23@@EndBracket@@ as Black is cut off by two files and the White King can hide behind his own pawn.  6...Ra7+  7.Kf6  Ra6+  8.e6  Rb6  9.Kf7 }
2. Rg7
{ With the idea of bringing the King up to e6, then meeting ...Re8+ with Re7 }
2... Kh5 3. Kf4 Rf8+
{ After   3...Kh6  4.Rg1  White is threatening to push e5. If Black tries to check us here, we will have the mating idea seen earlier  4...Rf8+  5.Ke5  Re8+  6.Kf6 }
4. Ke5 Re8+
{ 4...Kh6  to try and stop an eventual Ke6 then Re7  5.Rg1  Re8+  6.Kf6 } 5.
Kf5 Rf8+ 6. Ke6 Re8+ 7. Re7 Ra8 8. Kf6
{ White is ready to score a touchdown very soon, and can meet ...Rf8+ with Rf7 }
*

