{ If Black had a rook pawn and the White King were cut off by three files, White draws the game very easily. There are simply too many ways for him to obtain the half point, the most direct of which is to break the Black Rook's barrier by offering a Rook trade on e1, then f1. This enables White's King to inch towards Black’s pawn. }
1. Re1 Rf8 2. Ke2 h4 3. Rf1 Rh8 4. Kf2 h3 5. Kg3 h2 6. Rh1 *

