[White "5. Endgame Ideas"]
[Black "Zugzwang"]
[Result "*"]

{ A zugzwang is a situation in which the obligation to make a move in one's turn is a serious disadvantage. This happens most often in endgames because the defender will not have innocuous moves to pass the turn to the opponent.   You can think of zugzwang as the evil cousin of stalemate. In the case of stalemate, the defender is fortunate that his lack of freedom earns him a half point. Whereas for zugzwang, the losing side’s severe immobility leaves him with no choice other than a poor move.  Recall the two strategies one can use to cheat death with stalemate. The first involves jettisoning your pieces when your King’s movement is already restricted. The second requires you to actively trap your King and other pieces.   Therefore, we can also force our opponent into zugzwang by using exactly the same strategies – either punish your opponent when his position is already cramped, or find ways to limit his freedom. Now let’s practice creating zugzwangs. }
1. -- *

