{ Aside from time trouble, there are only three causes of calculation mistakes:  1. Dismissing Tactical Motifs  2. Unfamiliarity with Patterns  3. Poor Visualisation  These causes can be extremely costly. In this chapter, I will show some examples of miscalculations in action. At the end, I will wrap up the entire course with a summary of what you could do to further develop your chess calculation skill. }
